# Demo Videos Folder

Place your demoscene video captures here for playback on the LED matrix.

## Supported formats:
- .mp4 (recommended)
- .webm
- .mkv
- .avi
- .mov
- .flv

## Required on Linux:
FFmpeg must be installed:
```bash
sudo apt install ffmpeg
```

## Tips for best results:
1. Videos will be scaled to your matrix resolution automatically
2. Lower resolution source videos work best (less processing)
3. High contrast content looks best on LED matrices
4. Consider adding a MOD/XM soundtrack for authentic demoscene experience

## Where to find demo captures:
- https://pouet.net/ - The demoscene database
- https://demozoo.org/ - Archive with video links
- https://www.youtube.com/ - Search "demoscene" + demo name
- https://files.scene.org/ - Original demo files (need emulator to capture)

## Recording your own demos:
You can capture demos running in emulators:
- DOSBox for PC demos
- FS-UAE for Amiga demos
- Use OBS or FFmpeg to record the window
